

Graph preview workspaces:
Use bd show ID or bd show --id ID (equivalent to beads/ID) for a current Memory or
Issue; use bd show links/ID for a Link. Multiple positional/--id operands
show current Issues in the supplied order, with ordinary Issue JSON or human
details. Memory, Link, exact-version and graph-json reads remain single-ID.
--refs shows incoming Issue references, grouped by relationship; --children
shows only parent-child references. Both accept current Issue IDs and retain
the familiar human view or Issue-ID-keyed JSON object.
--watch follows one current Issue, redrawing its human detail view when that
Issue changes; stop it with Ctrl+C.
--current selects the actor's first in-progress Issue, then hooked Issue, then
the last-touched Issue; it cannot combine with an explicit ID.
ID@N selects the stable store-local revision number N. ID@=TOKEN or
'[URL]@=TOKEN' selects one exact retained record; --revision N or
--revision =TOKEN is an alternative (not both). @current reads current. Unwrapped URL forms containing :// are
literal, including raw @; use the full canonical Scope URL to escape local
@ shorthand. Colon-only forms such as plan:v1@=TOKEN use local syntax.
Bracketed operands require canonical HTTP(S) Scope URLs, not opaque URIs.
Suffixes are rejected on the selected update and deletion targets; use
--if-revision for write comparison. The flag forms require a positive local
ordinal N or =TOKEN; a bare token and current are not flag values.
Endpoint pins remain unavailable. This is not an ordered history listing.
A current Issue's
--json uses the ordinary detail array with Scope-relative Bead IDs and its
graph revision token. Memory, Link, and exact --revision reads use the
experimental graph envelope; --format graph-json explicitly requests that
envelope for a current Issue too. graph-json is not a BDP Resource format.
Showing an Issue makes it the last-touched Issue for interactive update/close;
showing a Memory or Link does not.

Usage:
  bd show [id...] [--id=<id>...] [--current] [flags]

Aliases:
  show, view

Flags:
      --as-of string                Show issue as it existed at a specific commit hash or branch (requires Dolt; commit hashes must be the full 32-character hash from 'bd history', not a prefix)
      --brief-deps                  Reduce each dependency to its identity fields in JSON output (--json only; drops description, design, notes and acceptance criteria)
      --children                    Show only the children of this issue
      --comments-tail int           Render only the last N comments in text output, preceded by one elision line naming how many older ones were hidden (text output only; 0, the default, renders every comment unchanged; N must be >= 0)
      --current                     Show the currently active issue (in-progress, hooked, or last touched)
      --format string               Output format: json (alias for --json), or graph-json for the experimental complete-record envelope
  -h, --help                        help for show
      --id stringArray              Issue ID (use for IDs that look like flags, e.g., --id=gt--xyz)
      --include stringArray         Include a JSON Pointer; repeat to union selections
      --include-comments            Stream full comment bodies in JSON output (--json only; may be slow on issues with many comments). Without it the comments field is absent entirely, not truncated: an issue with comments carries comment_count and comments_omitted=true, so check those before reading an absent comments field as none.
      --include-dependents          Stream full dependent issues in JSON output (--json only; may be slow on hub beads)
      --local-time                  Show timestamps in local time instead of UTC (date-only fields are always local)
      --long                        Show all available fields (extended metadata, agent identity, gate fields, etc.)
      --omit stringArray            Omit an optional JSON Pointer, or envelope for raw JSON; repeatable
      --output-format stringArray   Canonical output: default, detail or json (cannot combine with legacy --json or --format)
      --refs                        Show issues that reference this issue (reverse lookup)
      --revision string             Read retained revision N or =TOKEN (graph preview only)
      --short                       Show compact one-line output per issue
      --thread                      Show full conversation thread (for messages)
  -w, --watch                       Watch for changes and auto-refresh display

For global flags, run `bd --help`.
